From 000608043f3b2408d009066387922805443b5dd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozark <ozark@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:54:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Remote control: org.ozark.Dash1 for the phone app, pairing
 code on screen, Phone app list

ozark-remoted (remote/ in the Ozark OS repository) lets a phone app control
the radio over Wi-Fi or Bluetooth LE. Dash's part:

- org.ozark.Dash1 on the system bus (DashRemote): GetState() and
  StateChanged give volume, brightness, theme, the page and the media
  sources; Control(method, params) runs the remote protocol's dash.*,
  media.* and radio.* methods (volume, brightness, theme, page; play,
  pause, toggle, next, previous, source; tune, step, band, presets).
  Bad parameters come back as org.ozark.Dash1.Error.BadParams.
- MediaRemote: the Radio, Bluetooth and Local tabs report what they play
  (title, artist, position, radio band, station and presets) and act on
  the remote's requests. The source that played last gets play/pause.
  The radio's save-preset and play/stop became methods both use.
- ozark-remoted's PairingStarted puts the 6-digit code on screen with a
  countdown (cancel stops the pairing); PairingEnded closes it and says
  the phone is paired.
- Settings > Bluetooth lists the phones paired with the app ("Phone app"),
  connected or when last used, with "remove" (RevokeClient).

Also: the Bluetooth player's hint points at Settings > Bluetooth.
